// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/t27f/gnn_work_graph_viz.t27 -- the T27F GNN work-graph page of T27 OS (issue #12370, epic #12173).
; Built on specs/t27f/viz_contract.t27; the same one-state, one-reducer shape as petal_specs_viz.t27.
; --
; What it answers: "which embeddings would a k-layer GNN gather into this node?" The reader hovers a
; node (or clicks it to pin it) and the page lights its k-hop neighbourhood, dims the rest, and lists the
; nodes of each hop in a side panel. k is a control with three cells, 1..3. This is the t27 reading of
; the web page https://t27.ai/t27f/gnn/ (hero figure): the same 17-node, 17-edge work graph, the same
; opacities, the same gather text.
; --
; Data source: a FIXTURE written into this file (17 nodes: SPEC, AGENT, TASK, ACTION, ARTIFACT; 17 edges:
; READS, ASSIGNED, PERFORMS, PRODUCES, VERIFIES, BLOCKS), copied from the web page's WG_NODES and
; WG_EDGES, which were built to follow the semantics of specs/t27f/work_graph.t27. It is not a fetch of
; the running graph, so the page opens with truth VIZ_TRUTH_DEMO and (viz_may_claim) may not present its
; numbers as a result. The node-kind and edge-kind numbers (0..4, 0..5) are the ones work_graph.t27 uses,
; held here as local constants: no test links the two files, so a renumbering there is not caught here.
; --
; Layers of this spec:
;   L1 fixture    node kind, label, id, name and position; edge ends, kind and label; hand-read adjacency.
;   L2 layout     a pure function of the fixture: web units scaled by 8/5 into a 1900 x 1000 frame.
;   L3 reach      gnn_reach: breadth-first hops from a node out to k, undirected, with the discovery
;                 order of the web page (a queue, edges scanned in index order).
;   L4 oracle     gnn_oracle_row: distance by repeated relaxation over the edge list, written apart.
;   L5 state      the contract's VizState, nothing added: hover and select name a node, the param is k - 1.
;   L6 host map   hit tests, click / hover / key to events, the state in five u64 words, the host layout.
; --
; Integer only: no floats. Pixel geometry is in frame coordinates (the origin is the frame's top-left
; corner), so a hit test and gnn_host agree without an offset. Opacity is in thousandths.
; --
; The host is the MAP page of specs/t27os/glass_window.t27 (issue #12370). It draws what the layers above
; compute and maps pointer and key events to L6; it holds no viz logic of its own. Not claimed: no run of
; the app on a screen is recorded in this file.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).

